<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hanil plans 300 mln mark bond issue.</title>
<headline>Hanil plans 300 mln mark bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Hanil Bank said on Monday it plans to issue 300 million marks of fixed-rate bonds in Germany later this month.  </p>
<p>The bonds will mature in three years.</p>
<p>The issue, lead managed by Bayerische Landesbank of Germany, will be made at 28 basis points over London Interbank Offered Rate (LIBOR) including fees.</p>
<p>Hanil will swap the issue with U.S. dollars at a floating rate, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement did not give more details.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
